@* The whole group unavailable, which is upstream's example — every item disabled rather than one
   of them. The glyphs dim with the control because the label asks has-[:disabled] of the input it
   wraps; a <label> is never :disabled itself, so asking it directly dimmed nothing. *@
<ToggleGroup aria-label="Text style">
    <ToggleGroupItem Name="tgd" Value="bold" Disabled aria-label="Toggle bold">
        <Icon Name="bold" />
    </ToggleGroupItem>
    <ToggleGroupItem Name="tgd" Value="italic" Disabled aria-label="Toggle italic">
        <Icon Name="italic" />
    </ToggleGroupItem>
    <ToggleGroupItem Name="tgd" Value="underline" Disabled aria-label="Toggle underline">
        <Icon Name="underline" />
    </ToggleGroupItem>
</ToggleGroup>
